===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|geometry}} Of or relating to a [[cone]] or cones.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=1665-11-06|editor=w:Henry Oldenburg|title=[[s:Philosophical Transactions/Volume 1/Number 6#section9|An Account of Hevelius his Prodromus Cometicus, together with some Animadversions made upon it by a French Philosopher]]|journal=w:Philosophical Transactions|volume=I|number=6|passage=He anſwers, That this Motion is Conical; and judgeth, that by the ''Conick'' path all the ''Phænomena'' of Comets can, without any inconveniency, be readily ſolved; even of that, which (by Hiſtory) in fifty days, paſſed through more then the 12 Signs of the ''Zodiack''; And of that, which in two days run through eight Signs: and of another, which in 48 days poſted through all the Signs, ''contra ſeriem''.}}
# Shaped like a cone.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1624|author=w:Edmund Gunter|chapter=XIII|title=The Description and Vse of the Sector|url=https://archive.org/details/descriptionuseof000gunt|location=London|publisher=Williã Jones|page=149|passage=IN Planes neither equinoctiall nor polar, the equator will be a right line, the tropiques and other parallels of declination will be '''conicall''' ſections, ſome of them parabolicall, ſome ellipticall, but the moſt of them hyperbolicall.}}
# {{lb|en|cartography}} Describing a map [[projection]] in which [[meridian]]s are mapped to equally spaced lines radiating out from the apex and [[parallel]]s of latitude are mapped to circular arcs centred on the apex.

